    "text": "By Crawford Anderson ,\n1 hours ago If I had a dollar for every time I said \"Roth IRA,\" I could bribe my way to having a consistently good parking spot on campus and still have enough to retire tomorrow. Since I can't do either, I am telling the story of two fictional Charlotte students, 'Cole Morgan' and 'Hannah Robinson,' to break down how the account actually works. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
